00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:47.353
Of course we

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.055
prioritize our work

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.758
and for us, the priority are cases

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.661
where people civilians

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.896
were killed, injured

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.532
or ill treated in different manner.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:03.169
When they have been victims of harm,

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:07.440
sexual and any other type of attack

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:10.610
and prioritize these cases.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.344
Of course,

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:14.013
we the most challenging for us

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:16.082
is to identify the perpetrator

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.450
because many of them

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:20.553
are hiding their faces But for cases

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.788
we have already finished,

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.290
we not only identified the perpetrators,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.392
but we also collected evidence

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:29.128
that they initially committed

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.663
these war crimes.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.931
And hundreds

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.567
and thousands of cases are ongoing.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.602
And this is our primary job

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.905
to deliver justice to Ukrainians

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.239
in our national system

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:43.576
while we have already great results

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.945
in international level. Right.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:46.913
So you met with U.S.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:47.714
